okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Release the /ImportSession slash-command arguments parser fix to nightly and install the published nightly locally."
authorization: >
  User, 2026-10-17: explicit nightly push and local (current user only) deployment of the ImportSession parser fix:
  npm install -g of the exact published version and a fresh full-SHA snapshot through the published install.ps1.
  No remote or managed (G:) machine change, no live router, session or config change, no live snapshot overwrite.
status: "released to nightly and installed locally (current user); results below, added in the follow-up journal commit"
base: "nightly 1707ad4ddc6775f1005eaf40e3ece8df6c343d02 (CI 39000016160 and Publish 39000016191 success)"
diagnosis: "../../diagnostics/import-session/investigation.okf"
scope:
  production:
    - "ciel_runtime_support/request_shortcuts.py import_session_args: stop collecting the Arguments block at the first blank line once an argument is collected (4 added lines)."
  tests_new:
    - "tests/test_session_import_regression.py (synthetic fixtures only; joins the unit group by filename)."
  tests_modified:
    - "tests/test_request_shortcuts.py: shipped-template and paragraph-boundary regressions."
  release_owner_change:
    - "tests/test_session_import_regression.py test_byte_and_character_truncation: lambda `row` rewritten as a nested def. ruff E731 failed `ruff check .` (the Publish workflow step) on the original file. Same behavior; later line numbers shift by 2 relative to the diagnostics before.txt tracebacks."
  changelog: "CHANGELOG.md Unreleased entry '/ImportSession slash command'. It claims no MCP import tool and no new source format; neither exists (investigation.okf)."
lf_normalized_sha256_of_released_modules:
  request_shortcuts.py: "f8590f83bcc14c8ca5621d54e2df34ef838ddfc7cb5c21bb938d81a6bad0a86b"
  slash_command_assets.py: "f60600b4ded27404bfdcce6cda84e8dee577fdfef914db180b0b409ce81cea50 (unchanged)"
  session_import.py: "766230134b7186dd1380d7de2e7fcf9a30b6ed6ef1c528fcaaa9f6a73298f1f8 (unchanged)"
pre_push_verification:
  focused: "diagnostics/import-session/run_focused.py (4 files, 23 tests, inherited CIEL_RUNTIME_* removed, isolate_runtime_state): OK on Python 3.11 and 3.10.6 (CI python-minimum), and again on 3.10.6 after the E731 change."
  lint: "ruff 0.14.11 and the Publish-pinned ruff 0.15.22 (uvx, cache only): `ruff check .` All checks passed. git diff --check clean."
  groups: >
    scripts/run_test_group.py (Python 3.11.6, inherited CIEL_RUNTIME_* removed): unit 2062 OK (49 skipped),
    router 1334 OK, channel 462 OK (80 skipped), runtime 406 OK (19 skipped). The unit group was started before the
    E731 rewrite and may have loaded the earlier copy of test_session_import_regression.py; the focused run after the
    rewrite covers that file.
  docs_check: "npm run check:docs (CI quality step): Documentation metadata checks passed."
  live_health: "127.0.0.1:9385/9489/9505/9512 /health returned 200 before and after the test runs (status codes only)."
baseline_reproduction_note: >
  diagnostics/import-session/run_focused.py --baseline loads `git show HEAD:ciel_runtime_support/request_shortcuts.py`.
  After this commit HEAD carries the fix; the pre-fix parser is `1707ad4:ciel_runtime_support/request_shortcuts.py`.
release:
  commit: "890299d8ca78e10b294a97898fb70ef36482d935 (pushed 1707ad4..890299d to origin/nightly)"
  ci: "https://github.com/OneCielAI/ciel-runtime/actions/runs/39032072846 success (quality, python-minimum, test unit/router/channel/runtime)"
  publish: >
    https://github.com/OneCielAI/ciel-runtime/actions/runs/39032072760 success. Published
    0.2.51-nightly.20261017-122407.890299d with dist-tag nightly. The workflow's "Verify published tarball" step
    retried 60 times while the registry propagated and passed on attempt 61 (evidence/publish-run-extract.txt).
  registry: >
    npm view: version 0.2.51-nightly.20261017-122407.890299d, gitHead 890299d8ca78e10b294a97898fb70ef36482d935,
    dist-tags nightly=that version, latest=0.2.51 (evidence/registry-version.txt, registry-dist-tags.json).
  tarball: >
    npm pack of the exact version into a new empty directory: sha1 and sha512 equal registry dist.shasum and
    dist.integrity (evidence/local-tarball-digest.txt). LF-normalized comparison with git 890299d: 1692 of 1694 files
    identical; package.json and runtime_constants.py differ only by the CI version stamp
    (evidence/tarball-vs-git-summary.txt, tarball-fix-files.txt). Its install.ps1 equals the repository copy that was
    read before running it.
local_install:
  pre_state: >
    npm global @one-ciel-ai/ciel-runtime 0.2.51-nightly.20261017-034922.1707ad4; HKCU CIEL_RUNTIME_HOME
    C:\Users\djlov\.local\share\ciel-runtime-1707ad4ddc6775f1005eaf40e3ece8df6c343d02; user PATH first entry
    C:\Users\djlov\.local\bin. All 9 visible ciel_runtime.py processes ran from the 1707ad4 snapshot; none from the
    npm global directory (evidence/live-homes-before.txt).
  npm_global: >
    npm install -g @one-ciel-ai/ciel-runtime@0.2.51-nightly.20261017-122407.890299d (prefix
    C:\Users\djlov\AppData\Roaming\npm, inherited CIEL_RUNTIME_* removed; the package has no lifecycle scripts).
    Installed tree vs git: same 1692/1694 result, same stamp-only differences (evidence/npm-install-g.txt,
    npm-global-vs-git-summary.txt, npm-global-fix-files.txt).
  snapshot: >
    The tarball's install.ps1 run with pwsh 7.6.7 -NoProfile -File under its pre-existing RemoteSigned policy (no
    -ExecutionPolicy argument, no policy change; Windows PowerShell 5.1 is Restricted and was not used for it). The
    script has no Zone.Identifier stream. Environment: inherited CIEL_RUNTIME_* removed,
    CIEL_RUNTIME_INSTALL_HOME=C:\Users\djlov\.local\share\ciel-runtime-890299d8ca78e10b294a97898fb70ef36482d935 (new),
    PREFIX=C:\Users\djlov\.local. HKCU CIEL_RUNTIME_HOME now names that snapshot. The user Path registry value is
    byte-identical before and after (replayed cleanup predicted no write). Snapshot vs git: 424 of 425 identical,
    runtime_constants.py stamp only. The 11 .local\bin files the installer copies equal git and were already
    byte-identical to their previous contents. The 1707ad4 snapshot has no file newer than the release start
    (evidence/install-ps1.txt, pre-install-state.txt, hkcu-ciel-home-after.txt, snapshot-vs-git-summary.txt,
    snapshot-fix-files.txt, local-bin-vs-git.txt).
  launchers: >
    Run through cmd.exe with inherited CIEL_RUNTIME_* removed and an isolated scratch CIEL_RUNTIME_CONFIG_DIR, from an
    empty directory (cmd.exe searches the current directory before PATH): Roaming\npm\ciel-runtimectl.cmd version and
    .local\bin\ciel-runtimectl.cmd version both print ciel-runtime 0.2.51-nightly.20261017-122407.890299d. Under a PATH
    rebuilt from the Machine and User registry values (what a new terminal gets), `where ciel-runtimectl` lists
    .local\bin first and Roaming\npm second, and bare `ciel-runtimectl version` prints the same version. Shells started
    by the running session put Roaming\npm (position 11) before .local\bin (position 62); both now give the same
    version (evidence/launcher-versions.txt).
  observation: >
    `ciel-runtimectl version` writes workspace-router-ports.json and workspaces/<id>/telemetry-logs/ingest-token into
    the config directory when ciel_runtime.py is imported. That is why the launcher checks used a scratch config
    directory; those scratch directories are not committed.
functional_verification:
  composition_root: >
    evidence/scripts/installed_root_controller.py imports an installed ciel_runtime.py and calls its
    maybe_handle_import_session_request (the entry claude_router and openai_responses_router call) with the shipped
    IMPORT_SESSION_SLASH_COMMAND rendered for Codex/Claude, Windows paths containing spaces and the latest-transcript
    form. Codex requests are a Responses `input` body passed through the installed
    openai_responses_to_anthropic_messages first. HOME/USERPROFILE/CODEX_HOME point at a temporary home holding
    synthetic one-record transcripts; CIEL_RUNTIME_CONFIG_DIR is scratch with CIEL_RUNTIME_TEST_ISOLATED=1; python -I -B;
    the HTTP handler is an in-memory capture object.
    New snapshot 890299d: 4/4 HTTP 200 "Ciel Runtime ImportSession completed." containing the synthetic content.
    npm global 890299d: 4/4 the same. Old snapshot 1707ad4 (read only, no bytecode written): 4/4 "ImportSession failed:
    Transcript file not found: format and must be `Codex` or `Claude`." (evidence/functional/root-controller-*.json).
  support_layer: >
    evidence/scripts/installed_import_session.py wires the installed support modules the same way: 4/4 completed on the
    worktree, the new snapshot and npm global; 4/4 the error on the 1707ad4 snapshot (evidence/functional/harness-*.json).
  not_exercised: "A live router over a real socket, a real Claude Code or Codex client, and any real user transcript."
live_health:
  before: "11:58:01Z and 12:19:03Z: 9385, 9489, 9505, 9512 /health 200 (5 s timeout)."
  after: >
    9489, 9505 and 9512 /health 200 at 12:44:08Z and 12:46:07Z. 9385 gave no response within 5 s at 12:44:08Z and
    within 10 s at 12:46:07Z; other probes returned 200 in 7.3-8.2 s or in 8-13 ms. Over six probes 12:46:38Z-12:47:44Z
    all returned 200 (two in 7.3-7.7 s) and the 9385 listener stayed PID 72844 (python). Its start time, owner and command
    line are not readable from this account; earlier journals describe 9385 as the sandbox router. The cause of the
    slow or missing responses was not established. Nothing in this release starts, stops or configures that process
    (evidence/health-*.txt). The 9 visible ciel processes have the same PIDs before and after and still run from the
    1707ad4 snapshot (evidence/live-homes-after.txt); they keep that code until they are relaunched.
not_done:
  - "Running routers and CLI sessions were not restarted. No remote or managed machine was accessed."
not_claimed:
  - "No MCP import tool exists; importsession/ImportSession/import_session tools/call still return Unknown ciel-runtime-router tool."
  - "Muse transcripts are not an ImportSession source."
  - "The reporter's exact failed invocation was not supplied (investigation.okf Scope)."
